            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to publish, then the Bengali for an editor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: কথা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কথা — kôthā — \"words; talk; what someone said\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সাক্ষীর কথা শুনে দারোগা কিছু বললেন না। sākkhīr kôthā shune dārogā kichhu bôllen nā. The inspector listened to the witness and said nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কথা (kôthā) বলা, to talk; কথা (kôthā) দেওয়া, to give your word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কথা (kôthā) is Sanskrit kathā, 'talk, conversation; a story' (Monier-Williams), and it keeps both senses in Bengali."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
